<BaseLayout title="About KRIYANO | Developer & Web Utilities" description="Learn how KRIYANO builds focused browser-based utilities for developers, web work, data transformation and technical productivity.">
 <div class="container kit-page"><header class="kit-heading"><div class="section-kicker">About KRIYANO</div><h1>Small technical tools.<br/>Useful results.</h1><p>KRIYANO is shifting toward focused developer, web and data utilities that help people finish repetitive technical tasks quickly.</p></header>
 <article class="kit-reading"><h2>One clear job per tool</h2><p>The new KRIYANO toolkit is built around practical actions such as generating UUIDs, converting Unix timestamps, decoding JWT payloads, validating YAML, converting JSON/YAML, building cron expressions, encoding URLs and cleaning pasted data. The goal is to make common technical tasks quicker without unnecessary accounts or complicated workflows.</p><p>The idea behind the name comes from “Kriya”, or action. The goal remains the same: a result you can use immediately.</p>
 <h2>Browser-first where possible</h2><p>Many KRIYANO utilities are designed to process data locally in your browser. Each tool explains what it does, what it does not do and any important limitations. For example, the JWT Decoder can inspect a token's header and payload, but decoding does not verify its signature.</p>
 <h2>The AI prompt library is staying available</h2><p>KRIYANO previously focused on practical AI prompts and AI-assisted workflows. Those existing resources remain available during the transition, but they are no longer the primary direction of the site. We are preserving useful indexed URLs while the technical toolkit grows.</p>
 <h2>Clear about your data</h2><p>New local utilities such as the UUID Generator, Timestamp Converter, JWT Decoder, Base64 Encoder, YAML Validator and URL Encoder run in your browser. Some legacy features may work differently. See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for current details before entering sensitive information.</p>
 <h2>Help shape what comes next</h2><p>If there is a repetitive developer, web or data task that would benefit from a focused utility, send the suggestion to <a href="mailto:contact@kriyano.com">contact@kriyano.com</a>. Please avoid sending secrets, access tokens, credentials or confidential customer data.</p><div class="kit-actions"><a class="kit-btn primary" href="/tools/">Explore the tools →</a><a class="kit-btn" href="/contact/">Suggest a tool</a></div></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
